Multiple Linear Regression using Python and Scikit-learn
What is Multiple Linear Regression?

Multiple Linear Regression (MLR) is an extension of Simple Linear Regression where more than one independent variable (feature) is used to predict a dependent variable.

Simple Linear Regression

Uses only one input feature.

Example:

Salary = f(Years of Experience)
Multiple Linear Regression

Uses multiple input features.

Example:

House Price = f(Area, Bedrooms, Age, Location)

Y=β0​+β1​X1​+β2​X2​+β3​X3​+⋯+βn​Xn​

Y → Target (Dependent Variable)
β₀ → Intercept
β₁, β₂...βₙ → Coefficients
X₁, X₂...Xₙ → Independent Variables
Real-Life Example

Suppose we want to predict house price.

